Embedded React: less work per host element in the JavaScript bridge.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: bridges/quickjs/js/src/props.js and
bridges/quickjs/js/src/embedded-react/split-style.js.

Every host element the reconciler creates or updates goes through
splitAnimatedStyle and buildProps. buildProps looked each of the 40 passthrough
prop names up on the element's props, which carry a handful, so nearly every
lookup missed; it now walks the props it was given against a set of the same
names. splitAnimatedStyle copied a plain style object into a temporary before
copying it again; it now reads the object directly and flattens only arrays.
Same results. In a profile of a screen of cards mounting, buildProps was the
largest single self time.

--- a/bridges/quickjs/js/src/props.js
+++ b/bridges/quickjs/js/src/props.js
@@ -179,11 +179,15 @@
   return null;
 }
 
+const PASSTHROUGH_KEYS = new Set(PASSTHROUGH);
+
 export function buildProps(type, props, flatStyle) {
   const flat = flatStyle ? {...flatStyle} : {};
   if (!flatStyle) flattenStyle(props.style, flat);
-  for (const k of PASSTHROUGH) {
-    if (props[k] !== undefined) flat[k] = props[k];
+  // An element's props hold a handful of keys: checking each against the set costs far less than
+  // looking every passthrough name up on them, most of which they do not have.
+  for (const k in props) {
+    if (PASSTHROUGH_KEYS.has(k) && props[k] !== undefined) flat[k] = props[k];
   }
   // <Svg> takes width/height as DIRECT props (the react-native-svg convention) — the engine sizes the
   // vector node from them. Fold them into the resolved style (an explicit style width/height still wins)
